{% comment %}
  Questions & answers — the shopper-facing half.

  Why this block exists
  ---------------------
  The server side of Q&A has been complete for a long time: GET/POST
  /api/storefront/questions, plan gating, per-email dedupe, rate limiting, and a merchant
  moderation screen in the app. What was missing was any way for a shopper to reach it —
  no block, and no fetch in the widget script. `db.question.create` had exactly one caller
  and that caller was unreachable, so the merchant's Questions screen could only ever be
  empty while the feature was billed on the Growth plan.

  Design constraints, matching the review block for the same reasons:

  - **Reserved space.** A min-height is declared before any data arrives so the page does
    not shift when questions load. The script fills it with skeletons rather than letting
    it collapse, because a box that empties is a layout shift exactly like one that fills.
  - **Deferred load.** Nothing is fetched until the block nears the viewport. Q&A sits
    below reviews on almost every product page, so loading it eagerly is pure waste.
  - **Nothing is published without the merchant.** A submitted question lands unpublished
    and appears here only once answered and approved. A public form that writes straight to
    a storefront is a spam vector.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  comment
    Same colour precedence as review-list.liquid: emit an override ONLY when the merchant
    has moved a setting off its default. The script fills in any custom property that is
    not already set, so an untouched block emitting its defaults inline would silently
    outrank the colours chosen in the app, and Settings -> Display would appear dead.

    These defaults must match the schema below. Change one, change both.
  endcomment
  assign default_accent = '#059669'
  assign default_radius = 8

  assign style = ''
  if block.settings.accent_color != blank and block.settings.accent_color != default_accent
    assign style = style | append: '--rm-accent:' | append: block.settings.accent_color | append: ';'
  endif
  if block.settings.corner_radius != default_radius
    assign style = style | append: '--rm-radius:' | append: block.settings.corner_radius | append: 'px;'
  endif

  comment
    Reserved height is a layout hint about this placement, not a style choice, so unlike
    the colours above it always applies.
  endcomment
  assign style = style | append: '--rm-min-height:' | append: block.settings.reserved_height | append: 'px;'
-%}

<div
  id="reviewmaster-questions"
  class="rm-widget rm-questions"
  data-rm-questions
  data-rm-shop="{{ shop.permanent_domain }}"
  data-rm-product="{{ product.id }}"
  data-rm-app-url="{{ block.settings.app_url | default: 'https://reviewmaster-app.azurewebsites.net' | escape }}"
  style="{{ style }}"
  {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
>
  <h2 class="rm-widget__heading">{{ 'reviewmaster.questions_heading' | t }}</h2>

  {%- comment -%}
    Announcement region for "your question has been sent". Rendered up front, empty and
    hidden, because a live region only announces CHANGES — one inserted later with its
    text already set is not reliably read out. The script fills it and unhides it.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="rm-notice" data-rm-q-notice role="status" aria-live="polite" hidden></div>

  {%- comment -%}
    Always emitted, but HIDDEN until the app confirms this store accepts questions.

    Theme app blocks are offered to every store with the app installed, regardless of
    plan, and Liquid has no way to know the plan. Rendering the button live meant a Free
    store advertised "Ask a question" and rejected every submission — after the shopper
    had typed their name, email and a paragraph. The script reveals it only when the
    questions API reports canAsk. Still always in the markup rather than conditional on a
    theme setting: a theme that can remove the element leaves the app-side switch with
    nothing to show.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="rm-questions__actions">
    <button type="button" class="rm-btn rm-btn--primary" data-rm-q-open aria-expanded="false" hidden>
      {{ 'reviewmaster.ask_question' | t }}
    </button>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    min-height reserves the space, and the skeletons occupy it so the box is never a blank
    gap — including when the extension script fails to run, which on a theme with a broken
    script tag is not hypothetical. The script replaces these on load and releases the
    height once real content is in place. role="list" carries the structure for assistive
    tech; the visual Q/A markers the script renders are hidden from it.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="rm-q-list" data-rm-q-list role="list" aria-busy="true" style="min-height: var(--rm-min-height);">
    <div class="rm-q rm-q--skeleton" aria-hidden="true">
      <span class="rm-skel rm-skel--line"></span>
      <span class="rm-skel rm-skel--line rm-skel--short"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="rm-q rm-q--skeleton" aria-hidden="true">
      <span class="rm-skel rm-skel--line"></span>
      <span class="rm-skel rm-skel--line rm-skel--short"></span>
    </div>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    Hidden until asked for. Most visitors read rather than write, so the form should cost
    them nothing.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="rm-form-wrap" data-rm-q-form-wrap hidden>
    <form class="rm-form" data-rm-q-form novalidate>
      <h3 class="rm-form__title">{{ 'reviewmaster.ask_question' | t }}</h3>

      {%- comment -%}
        Honeypot. Hidden from humans, irresistible to bots. tabindex and autocomplete off so
        keyboard and password-manager users never land in it. The server treats a filled
        `website` field as automated and answers 200 without writing anything, so the bot
        records a success and does not adapt.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="rm-hp" aria-hidden="true">
        <label>Website<input type="text" name="website" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off"></label>
      </div>

      <label class="rm-form__field">
        <span>{{ 'reviewmaster.your_name' | t }}</span>
        <input type="text" name="name" required maxlength="100" autocomplete="name">
      </label>

      <label class="rm-form__field">
        <span>{{ 'reviewmaster.your_email' | t }}</span>
        <input type="email" name="email" maxlength="200" autocomplete="email">
        <small>{{ 'reviewmaster.question_email_privacy' | t }}</small>
      </label>

      <label class="rm-form__field">
        <span>{{ 'reviewmaster.your_question' | t }}</span>
        <textarea name="body" required rows="4" maxlength="2000"></textarea>
      </label>

      <div class="rm-form__actions">
        <button type="submit" class="rm-btn rm-btn--primary">{{ 'reviewmaster.submit_question' | t }}</button>
        <button type="button" class="rm-btn rm-btn--ghost" data-rm-q-cancel>{{ 'reviewmaster.cancel' | t }}</button>
      </div>

      <p class="rm-form__status" data-rm-q-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
    </form>
  </div>
</div>

{%- comment -%}
  No manual <script> tag: declaring "javascript" in the schema makes Shopify serve the
  asset from its CDN, deduplicated across blocks — so a page carrying both the review block
  and this one loads reviewmaster.js once, not twice. Adding a tag as well double-loads it.
{%- endcomment -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Questions & answers",
  "target": "section",
  "stylesheet": "reviewmaster.css",
  "javascript": "reviewmaster.js",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Appearance",
      "info": "Overrides the colours set in the app, for this placement only. Leave at the defaults to use your app-wide settings."
    },
    { "type": "color", "id": "accent_color", "label": "Accent colour", "default": "#059669" },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "corner_radius",
      "label": "Corner radius",
      "min": 0, "max": 24, "step": 2, "unit": "px", "default": 8
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "reserved_height",
      "label": "Reserved height",
      "min": 0, "max": 600, "step": 50, "unit": "px", "default": 150,
      "info": "Space held before questions load, to prevent the page jumping. Set close to the typical rendered height."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Advanced"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "app_url",
      "label": "App URL",
      "default": "https://reviewmaster-app.azurewebsites.net",
      "info": "Leave this alone unless ReviewMaster support asks you to change it."
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
